  "implementation": {
    "admission": "Four source-selected profiles; legacy dynamic_plasma and zenon_funding remain thirteen/version1. Only named retained profiles select seventy-eight/eighteen/version2. Each actual native owner creates one private admission counter, claims before native capability creation, and offers no reset/refund.",
    "dpOwner": "A distinct actual bounded HTTPS owner per endpoint, composed with the existing actual Dynamic Plasma wire. No injected owner factory and no default buyer replacement.",
    "accountOwner": "The same actual native owner composed with the selected account exchange gate. Only canonical original JSON-RPC bodies with IDs one through eighteen, one checksum-valid user address, and the two existing account methods are forwarded.",
    "gate": "Captures exact DATA methods, rejects proxies/accessors without hooks, preserves body bytes and original Promise/close identity. It neither authenticates outcomes nor brands a borrowed owner. Rejection prehandling and native close remain the supplied actual owner's duties.",
    "descriptor": "Legacy funding policy remains version1 without a new admission member. Version2 retained policy records its explicit profile, count and single-contextv7 purpose. The optional policy receiver remains restricted to the old funding profile.",
    "noImplicitRenewal": "Creating a new volatile owner or repeating a raw ID does not grant continuation/retry/replacement authority. The count alone is not durable process-wide attempt identity."
  },
